<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis steady but undertone weak.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis steady but undertone weak.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal basis levels were mostly steady on Friday although the market had a weak undertone as it struggled to absorb the current fast crush pace.</p>
<p>Dealers noted the National Oilseed Processors Association put the crush for the week to January 1 at a stronger-than- expected 30.58 million bushels. Most had expected it to be little changed from the previous week's 29.69 million.</p>
<p>&quot;That is a very large crush for a holiday-shortened week,&quot; one dealer said, noting sluggish demand was also weighing on basis levels.  </p>
